    <sys:String x:Key="GameMode.WhatTitle">What happens when you turn it on</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GameMode.What1">Power: the High performance power plan becomes active. If it does not exist, as on many laptops, the power mode is set to Best performance.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GameMode.What2">Background load: Windows Search indexing and Delivery Optimization are paused. Both otherwise cause disk and network load.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GameMode.What3">Windows Update is paused for one week so no update downloads or restarts in the middle of a game.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GameMode.Note">Game Mode runs without a background program and stays on after a restart until you turn it off. Turning it off restores the previous power plan, restarts the services and resumes Windows Update.</sys:String>
